{"version":"1","id":"an0n_ali","handle":"an0n_ali","name":"An0n Ali","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--FDbuqNiP--/f_auto/v1723788734/logos/an0n_ali","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.778,"y":-7.9955,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":66,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-05T13:07:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-06-28T11:25:35.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.143939,"listicle_ratio":0.045455,"question_ratio":0.151515,"avg_read_time":4.5,"summary_length_avg":430.896552,"title_length_avg":42.348485,"title_length_var":131.469467,"tag_entropy":2.364707,"tag_diversity":0.530303,"top_tag_share":0.227273,"avg_upvotes":5.30303,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.121212,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.025641,"zero_engagement_share":0.515152,"viral_share":0.015152,"posts_per_week":0.736491,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.178571},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[4.7647,-2.1471],"cadence_depth":[-2.5735,-3.5588],"hype_variety":[9.6618,-7.4265],"title_style":[9.4412,7.9559]},"top_tags":[["cyber",54],["security",49],["linux",32],["osint",10],["ai",5],["malware",4],["privacy",4],["social-media",3]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Learning Python Basics to Enhance Hacking Skills","20 Browser Extensions for HACKERS & OSINT!","How to Use AI for OSINT?"],"outlier":["Essential cybersecurity tools for ethical hacking and penetration testing"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"aOU86u1Sz","title":"Encryption Explained in 30 Seconds","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bvMzCKQm4Zg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/encryption-explained-in-30-seconds-aou86u1sz","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bvMzCKQm4Zg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-02T13:07:00.000Z"},{"id":"SdsV7LPQa","title":"Encryption Basics for Hackers","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wi051byN1DY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/encryption-basics-for-hackers-sdsv7lpqa","summary":"A beginner-friendly explainer covering how encryption works, from symmetric and asymmetric encryption basics to the four main ways hackers bypass it: stealing encryption keys, exploiting implementation flaws (poor key storage, hardcoded keys, backdoors), protocol-level attacks (SSL stripping, man-in-the-middle), and brute force/dictionary attacks against weak passwords. Uses simple analogies to explain public/private key exchange and how HTTPS and end-to-end encryption function in practice.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wi051byN1DY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:53:00.000Z"},{"id":"Wc6iqCLEv","title":"What is Social Media Intelligence?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YZ-SMoRMdzg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-social-media-intelligence--wc6iqclev","summary":"Open-source intelligence (OSINT) is a technique used by security researchers, hackers, and law enforcement to gather publicly available information about targets. Using a practical example, it demonstrates how social media photos can be geolocated by combining image cleanup tools (like cleanup.picture) with reverse image search on Yandex to identify locations even from partially obscured images. This serves as an introduction to a specific OSINT branch called Social Media Intelligence (SOCMINT).","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YZ-SMoRMdzg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-02T13:50:00.000Z"},{"id":"Jd7LEcS1T","title":"How Hackers Target Power Grids and Water Plants","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EOnU3RjDiJs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-hackers-target-power-grids-and-water-plants-jd7lecs1t","summary":"An overview of how SCADA systems controlling critical infrastructure like power grids, water plants, and nuclear facilities are targeted by hackers. Uses real-world examples including the 2017 petrochemical plant attack and the 2021 Florida water plant breach to illustrate how these industrial control systems are exploited in cyber warfare.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EOnU3RjDiJs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-01T13:30:11.000Z"},{"id":"GGOFFClXu","title":"Why YouTube hacking tutorials won't make you a skilled hacker","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dMak7_Oeszk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-watching-youtube-videos-won-t-make-you-a-hacker-ggoffclxu","summary":"Watching short YouTube tutorials on hacking tools gives only a narrow, single-phase view of what real hacking involves. Skilled hackers rely on creative thinking across multiple attack phases rather than tool knowledge alone. Understanding the full lifecycle of a system compromise is what separates a script kiddie from a professional penetration tester.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dMak7_Oeszk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-31T13:35:01.000Z"},{"id":"Lbs9PVSSq","title":"Getting started with Metasploit for penetration testing","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0opJl5_CpWY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-tool-every-pentester-uses-lbs9pvssq","summary":"An introduction to Metasploit, a widely used penetration testing framework. Covers its three main interfaces (MSF console, Armitage, and MSF Web), and explains how pentesters use it alongside network scanning tools like Nmap to identify open ports, match services to known vulnerabilities, and gain access to systems during authorized security assessments.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0opJl5_CpWY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-30T14:25:01.000Z"},{"id":"bJVCqXbH2","title":"How social engineering tricks people into giving up their passwords","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NUgjVDjrSHg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-hackers-steal-passwords-without-hacking-bjvcqxbh2","summary":"Social engineering is a manipulation technique used by hackers to extract sensitive information like passwords without any technical hacking. By exploiting psychological vulnerabilities and human trust, attackers can trick people into revealing credentials through simple conversation. The post walks through a real-world demonstration and explains the psychological flaws that make people susceptible to these attacks.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NUgjVDjrSHg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-29T13:50:01.000Z"},{"id":"xhSd4HRqL","title":"How software-defined radio is used to hack wireless devices","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRtkZ-DrSOs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-wireless-devices-get-hacked-xhsd4hrql","summary":"An overview of how software-defined radio (SDR) can be used to intercept and exploit radio frequency signals from everyday wireless devices such as car door locks and drone systems. SDR combines specialized hardware and software to capture any radio frequency, enabling attackers to compromise improperly secured devices.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SRtkZ-DrSOs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-28T13:33:00.000Z"},{"id":"mkzUY7VhH","title":"Why hackers learn Linux first","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ysHDJyyqkXY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-every-hacker-learns-linux-first-mkzuy7vhh","summary":"A beginner-oriented introduction to why Linux is the go-to operating system for aspiring hackers and cybersecurity learners. Covers the open-source nature of Linux, its prevalence in cybersecurity lab environments, and teases foundational topics like terminal basics, user management, the Linux file system, and the sudo command.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ysHDJyyqkXY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-27T15:37:34.000Z"},{"id":"DQtKXSBW9","title":"Why Hackers Get Caught! (Bad OPSEC)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZwAtuAbmg8","co